Most bindings should stay immutable. Add `~` when the value needs to change.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    count ~= 0
    ~count = 1
    ~count += 1
]

Prefix the whole target with `~` when writing to an existing mutable place.

Collections also need a mutable binding before they can change:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    names ~{String} = {}

    ~names.push("Priya")
]

The `~` before `names.push` requests exclusive access for that call. It is
separate from the `~` that made the binding mutable.
